{
  "_comment": [
    "PRD 0050 RF3.3, PRD 0035 re-validation S-01: which texts a user language pack may replace.",
    "Read by cuotai_core::user_pack (embedded), the desktop crate's tests and scripts/test-*-ui.mjs. The TUI is out of scope: packs never reach it.",
    "Rules: an exact id, or a prefix ending in '*' ('settings.vault.*'; 'dialog.delete*' for camelCase leaves). The longest match wins and an exact id beats any prefix.",
    "An id that matches no rule is PROTECTED, and so is any id with a 'confirm' or 'consent' dot-segment, whatever matches. A new namespace is protected until someone classifies it.",
    "Tests: every shipped id (core catalogs in 'core', desktop UI catalogs in 'ui') matches a rule explicitly, and no rule is in both lists of a section. An id in both layers takes the strictest class.",
    "An id is protected when its text appears in, or describes: (1) a destructive confirmation (remove, delete, erase, revoke, overwrite, 'save anyway', turn off and erase);",
    "(2) a consent or disclosure (what is read, stored, sent, or where it goes; 'not a charge'); (3) a billed-query or cost warning;",
    "(4) a security or privacy warning (certificate trust, plain HTTP, file permissions, residual risk, hidden names); (5) the sign-in, paste-session, secret-entry and credential dialogs, and the move-to-vault flow;",
    "(6) the update prompt, the first-run permission prompt, the backup and restore dialogs; (7) permission texts (notifications, system settings) and the local-server, hooks, extensions and channels settings;",
    "(8) every title, button, checkbox and error shown inside those dialogs and panels (they use their own 'confirm.*' button ids, not 'common.*'); (9) the notices about user content itself ('userContent.*').",
    "A UI id that apps/desktop/ui/js/desktop-wording.js maps a protected core text onto is protected too, and listed explicitly (scripts/test-desktop-wording-ui.mjs checks it).",
    "Everything else is overridable, and only through a rule in 'overridable'."
  ],
